text: >-
  From:

  Sent: Thursday, November 20, 2025 10:23 PM

  To: Candace Tips <moretips@candaceowens.com>

  Subject: Minot, ND IMPORTANT

  Candace,

  military member (one of the good ones). I think one of the keys to not
  overlook is BTTs stopover in Minot, ND. Why stop there at all on the 4th? Why
  not fly

  direct to Provo? Not only does Minot have an FBI Office, but it also has an
  Air Force Base. Among other tenants, that Air Force Base is home to the 891st
  Missile Security

  Forces Squadron, a combined military and civilian security force that had just
  come off of Operation Valhalla, a training exercise in Minnesota from 24-29
  Aug where the security

  forces practiced long range shooting practice among other things. Remember on
  Sep 12 when Kash Patel ended his press conference with "Lastly, to my friend
  Charlie Kirk:

  Rest now my brother. We have the watch, and I'll see you in Valhalla..."? Very
  interesting thing to say. I don't believe in coincidences.

  Minot is also home to Global Strike Command, which has worked with Israel on
  joint exercises such as Juniper Oak. France has also partnered with the 5th
  bomber wing at

  Minot. So although I haven't found anything to say that Israel or France was
  on that base or on that plane that day, they have worked with the Global
  Strike Command in the

  past.

  My theory is that at least part of the team you are looking for may have
  boarded the plane in Minot. Stopping in North Dakota for 1 hour just doesn't
  make sense. Are they going

  to say it was a fuel stop? It would be nice to check whether that plane has
  enough fuel to fly from Paris to Provo direct.

  I have attached some screenshots of google searches that anyone can do for
  verification. Let's catch these evil mfs!

  Btw, sent you an earlier email about google trends data that I also think is
  interesting.

  Keep up the hard work and here to help in any way I can,

  Best,

  Landlace
